Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 16:22:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] Route INT8 linear by ROCm architecture

One automatic INT8 linear backend was not optimal
across the tested ROCm architectures.

Reason:
- Triton was faster than AITER on gfx90a and gfx1100.
- AITER was slightly faster than Triton on gfx1201.
- Explicit AITER overrides must remain available.

Fix:
- Prefer Triton automatically on gfx90a and gfx1100.
- Continue selecting AITER automatically on gfx1201.
- Preserve explicit `--linear-backend=aiter` requests.

Testing
- Pass 12 scaled-MM kernel-selection tests.
- gfx90a: Triton 101.27, AITER 97.91 tokens/s.
- gfx1100: Triton 97.29, AITER 85.33 tokens/s.
- gfx1201: Triton 120.63, AITER 123.23 tokens/s.
- Final gfx1201 matrix reached 123.08 tokens/s.

Tools used:
- GPT-5.6 Sol: coding agent

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
---
 .../test_scaled_mm_kernel_selection.py        | 60 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../kernels/linear/scaled_mm/aiter.py         | 14 +++++
 2 files changed, 74 insertions(+)

